+The first list is the actual _orBool_ truth table in input order
+(false,false), (false,true), (true,false), (true,true). The second list is
+actual notBool_ on false and true. The file also machine-checks equal and
+unequal SortK witnesses, a satisfiable unequal-Value guard witness, and three
+counterfactual convenience bridges. The counterfactual theorems show that a
+right projection for orBool, a constant-true equality, or a constant-false
+negation can satisfy the generated equation; consequently the operational
+bridge comparison is independently load-bearing.
